WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:03.601
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:08.133
You guys,
it is Veterans Day,

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:10.501
and, tonight,
our entire audience is made up

00:00:10.501 --> 00:00:14.467
of veterans, active military,
and military families.

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:16.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:23.634
♪♪

00:00:23.634 --> 00:00:24.701
Please, have a seat.

00:00:24.701 --> 00:00:26.400
Welcome, welcome,
welcome, welcome.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.634
That's right. It's just like our
Fleet Week audience but sober.

00:00:29.634 --> 00:00:32.734
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.734 --> 00:00:35.234
All kidding aside, I want to say
thank you for your service.

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:38.033
You truly are the bravest.
Thank you.

00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:39.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:43.467
I mean it.
The closest most of us have come

00:00:43.467 --> 00:00:46.501
to a war zone is shopping
on Black Friday at TJ Maxx.

00:00:46.501 --> 00:00:47.901
[ Laughter ]
"Give that to me!

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:49.834
It's not even my size."

00:00:49.834 --> 00:00:52.501
Yep, the only people who have
seen more combat than you guys

00:00:52.501 --> 00:00:54.501
are flight attendants
on Southwest.

00:00:54.501 --> 00:00:58.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.234 --> 00:01:01.000
I remember -- I remember telling
my dad that I thought

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.167
a life in uniform
might be right for me,

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:05.701
so he went out and got me
a job application for Pizza Hut.

00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:08.167
[ Laughter ]
-Oh.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:10.567
Sadly, they said no.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.567 --> 00:01:13.000
Of course, the Space Force
couldn't be here tonight.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.534
They're busy --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:24.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:24.133 --> 00:01:26.701
They're busy monitoring
the galaxy for missiles,

00:01:26.701 --> 00:01:29.267
aliens, and our newest threat,
bored billionaires.

00:01:29.267 --> 00:01:33.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.968
A lot of restaurants
offered special deals today.

00:01:35.968 --> 00:01:38.901
Servicemembers could get a free
bloomin' onion at Outback.

00:01:38.901 --> 00:01:40.634
[ Cheers ]

00:01:40.634 --> 00:01:43.067
Free pancakes at IHOP.
[ Cheers ]

00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:44.767
And a free doughnut
at Krispy Kreme.

00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:46.067
[ Cheers ]

00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:48.000
And if you ate all three,
we have an ambulance outside

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.801
standing by, so don't worry.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:50.801 --> 00:01:52.200
Let's get to the news.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:55.033
The Postmaster General just said
that the U.S. Postal Service

00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:58.067
is ready for
the holiday-package rush.

00:01:58.067 --> 00:01:59.534
Unfortunately, the holiday
they're talking about

00:01:59.534 --> 00:02:00.801
is July 4th.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.801 --> 00:02:03.033
But still, they're ready.

00:02:03.033 --> 00:02:05.367
That's right.
The post office is prepared,

00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:07.100
meaning they "prepared" hundreds
of signs that say

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.701
"Next window please."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.701 --> 00:02:11.634
That's right. They said that
they're ready for the rush.

00:02:11.634 --> 00:02:13.868
Although I don't know how I feel
about the new slogan,

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:16.467
"United States Postal Service:
We can handle your package."

00:02:16.467 --> 00:02:17.767
[ Laughter ]
-Oh.

00:02:17.767 --> 00:02:19.367
-You can't say that.
-Why would you say that?

00:02:19.367 --> 00:02:21.767
-You can't say that anymore.
You can't --

00:02:21.767 --> 00:02:23.734
♪♪

00:02:23.734 --> 00:02:26.334
-Package.

00:02:26.334 --> 00:02:28.801
-Some business news.
The tuna lawsuit

00:02:28.801 --> 00:02:31.734
against Subway,
the sandwiches, is back.

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:35.367
Yeah, and now, they're saying
that the tuna contains chicken,

00:02:35.367 --> 00:02:38.834
pork, and cattle DNA.
[ Audience groans ]

00:02:38.834 --> 00:02:41.267
Even crazier, when they tested
Subway's chicken and pork,

00:02:41.267 --> 00:02:43.100
they found it was 100% tuna.
-Really?

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:46.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.701 --> 00:02:49.300
-Yep, chicken, pork,
and cattle DNA.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.534
Right now, Subway's thinking,

00:02:50.534 --> 00:02:52.234
"All things considered,
not bad."

00:02:52.234 --> 00:02:53.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.634 --> 00:02:54.934
"They're all meats, right?"

00:02:54.934 --> 00:02:57.167
Yep, Subway's like,
"What do you want from us?

00:02:57.167 --> 00:02:59.000
It's fish served
with an ice-cream scoop.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.200
Come on.
What do you want?"

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:01.801
[ Laughter ]
It's not like Morimoto's

00:03:01.801 --> 00:03:03.968
sharpening his knives
back there, cutting it up.

00:03:03.968 --> 00:03:08.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.734 --> 00:03:12.100
Well, I read that the CEO
of Royal Caribbean said that

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.267
the company is seeing
historically strong bookings

00:03:14.267 --> 00:03:16.367
for cruises next summer.

00:03:16.367 --> 00:03:17.934
Right now, members of
the Coast Guard and Navy

00:03:17.934 --> 00:03:19.100
are looking at each other, like,

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:21.067
"So, you guys gonna handle this,
or should we?"

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:22.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.734 --> 00:03:24.801
Meanwhile, Carnival Cruises
still hasn't let people

00:03:24.801 --> 00:03:26.567
off the boats from March 2020.

00:03:26.567 --> 00:03:29.267
[ Laughter and applause ]
"No, not yet.

00:03:29.267 --> 00:03:31.400
Not looking good.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.901
More tuna!"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:35.567
That's right, Royal Caribbean
said it's expecting

00:03:35.567 --> 00:03:38.200
record profits,
and then the CEO of Imodium

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:44.100
was like, "Same here."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.167
Some --
[ Chuckles ]

00:03:46.167 --> 00:03:48.133
Some air -- thank you.
Some airline --

00:03:48.133 --> 00:03:50.534
Some airline news.
The FAA has proposed

00:03:50.534 --> 00:03:55.667
more than $200,000 in fines
for 10 unruly passengers.

00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:57.000
Yeah.
And this is nice.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.033
Starting today,
if you're flying from Florida,

00:03:59.033 --> 00:04:01.000
they ask if you want
to pre-pay your fine.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.801
-Aww.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.801 --> 00:04:06.400
-"Hold my -- Hold my Four Loko.
That's unbelievable!"

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.934 --> 00:04:11.567
Get this -- I read that
a new survey found that 80%

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:14.567
of Americans use slang words
but only half

00:04:14.567 --> 00:04:17.033
know what the slang terms
they use actually mean.

00:04:17.033 --> 00:04:18.734
[ Laughter ]
Those aren't great numbers,

00:04:18.734 --> 00:04:20.167
so I thought
I'd help everyone brush up

00:04:20.167 --> 00:04:22.701
on their slang definitions
with a tiny song.

00:04:22.701 --> 00:04:30.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:30.868 --> 00:04:35.000
[ Tapping ]

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:38.968
♪ Acting extra
means "over the top" ♪

00:04:38.968 --> 00:04:42.634
♪ Spill the tea means
you should share the goss ♪

00:04:42.634 --> 00:04:44.000
♪ Receipts are proof ♪

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.767
♪ If you seem sus,
sus is short for suspicious ♪

00:04:46.767 --> 00:04:49.100
♪ Gucci's cool
and flex is showing off ♪

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:50.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.567 --> 00:04:54.300
♪ Curves is when you ignore
a flirty text ♪

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:58.067
♪ No cap means "for real,"
"We move" means "yes" ♪

00:04:58.067 --> 00:04:59.801
♪ Simping's
when you like someone ♪

00:04:59.801 --> 00:05:01.734
♪ But do too much for them ♪

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:04.367
♪ And simps are almost stans
but just not -- ♪

00:05:04.367 --> 00:05:06.601
Dang! Sorry.
Let me do it one more time.

00:05:06.601 --> 00:05:09.501
Can I do it one more time?
Hoo! All right, I'm close.

00:05:09.501 --> 00:05:11.000
[ Laughter ]

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.734
Yeah, don't waste your time
clapping because who knows

00:05:12.734 --> 00:05:13.934
how many takes
I got to do this.

00:05:13.934 --> 00:05:16.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:16.334 --> 00:05:18.400
Be exhausted.
-Go wash your hands.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:22.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:22.567 --> 00:05:24.567
You'll be asleep by the time --
Oh, here we go.

00:05:24.567 --> 00:05:26.767
-My hands are numb.
-All right, here we go.

00:05:26.767 --> 00:05:29.701
[ Tapping ]

00:05:29.701 --> 00:05:31.767
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.767 --> 00:05:33.901
Oh, yeah.
♪ Acting ♪

00:05:33.901 --> 00:05:36.334
[ Taps ]
Oh.

00:05:36.334 --> 00:05:37.534
-I thought
I was having a stroke.

00:05:37.534 --> 00:05:38.634
I didn't know
what was happening.

00:05:38.634 --> 00:05:40.133
[ Laughter ]
-Oh.

00:05:40.133 --> 00:05:42.968
-I had IHOP pancakes.
I had a Krispy Kreme.

00:05:42.968 --> 00:05:44.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.234 --> 00:05:46.834
All right, here we go.
[ Tapping ]

00:05:46.834 --> 00:05:49.200
♪ Acting extra -- ♪
Nope.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:52.000
Sorry, bud.
♪ Acting extra -- ♪

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:54.567
Yeah, there you go.
All right, here we go.

00:05:54.567 --> 00:05:55.667
Ready?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:55.667 --> 00:05:57.234
[ Tapping ]

00:05:57.234 --> 00:06:01.200
♪ Acting extra
means over the top ♪

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:04.868
♪ Spill the tea means
you should share the goss ♪

00:06:04.868 --> 00:06:06.234
♪ Receipts are proof ♪

00:06:06.234 --> 00:06:08.834
♪ If you seem sus,
sus is short for suspicious ♪

00:06:08.834 --> 00:06:12.834
♪ Gucci's cool,
and flex is showing off ♪

00:06:12.834 --> 00:06:14.167
You don't have
to be silent, either.

00:06:14.167 --> 00:06:16.634
I mean, you can --
[ Laughter ]

00:06:16.634 --> 00:06:18.934
Like a funeral, for God's sake.

00:06:18.934 --> 00:06:21.367
Did someone die?
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:21.367 --> 00:06:24.868
Jesus.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.868 --> 00:06:27.100
-I was hearing --
I was hearing tapping from --

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:28.868
I was hearing tapping
from the 10th floor!

00:06:28.868 --> 00:06:30.334
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.334 --> 00:06:31.567
Gosh.

00:06:31.567 --> 00:06:33.834
You said, "Don't clap."
-I did say, "Don't clap."

00:06:33.834 --> 00:06:36.200
Yeah, I -- Why am I gonna say,
"Don't clap"?

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:38.200
-You said no clapping.
-Clap. Do whatever you want.

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:39.534
You didn't say laugh.

00:06:39.534 --> 00:06:41.968
-I could hear someone
chewing gum, it was so quiet.

00:06:41.968 --> 00:06:44.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:44.734 --> 00:06:46.701
And it was off beat, too!
That was the worst part.

00:06:46.701 --> 00:06:50.434
[ Laughter ]

00:06:50.434 --> 00:06:51.667
-All right,
I'm gonna get this now.

00:06:51.667 --> 00:06:53.801
[ Laughter ]

00:06:53.801 --> 00:06:55.067
[ Tapping ]

00:06:55.067 --> 00:06:57.667
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.667 --> 00:07:01.634
♪ Acting extra
means over the top ♪

00:07:01.634 --> 00:07:05.200
♪ Spill the tea means
you should share the goss ♪

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:06.567
♪ Receipts are proof ♪

00:07:06.567 --> 00:07:09.467
♪ If you seem sus,
sus is short for suspicious ♪

00:07:09.467 --> 00:07:12.167
♪ Gucci's cool,
and flex is showing off ♪

00:07:12.167 --> 00:07:13.434
[ Cheers ]

00:07:13.434 --> 00:07:17.100
♪ Curve's when you ignore
a flirty text ♪

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:20.901
♪ No cap means for real,
"We move" means "yes" ♪

00:07:20.901 --> 00:07:22.767
♪ Simping's when
you like someone ♪

00:07:22.767 --> 00:07:24.701
♪ But do too much for them ♪

00:07:24.701 --> 00:07:27.334
♪ And simps are almost stans
but not quite yet ♪

00:07:27.334 --> 00:07:28.734
[ Cheers ]

00:07:28.734 --> 00:07:32.133
♪ "Slept on" means
something deserves more heat ♪

00:07:32.133 --> 00:07:34.767
♪ And if you want to say
woo-hoo say yeet ♪

00:07:34.767 --> 00:07:35.968
-Yeet!

00:07:35.968 --> 00:07:37.968
-♪ So now you know
the slang to drop ♪

00:07:37.968 --> 00:07:39.734
♪ The next time that you speak ♪

00:07:39.734 --> 00:07:42.501
♪ These all will be outdated
by next week ♪

00:07:42.501 --> 00:07:45.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:45.567 --> 00:07:49.033
♪♪

00:07:49.033 --> 00:07:51.367
-No, no, no!

00:07:51.367 --> 00:07:56.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:59.801
-Thank you.
[ Both laugh ]

00:07:59.801 --> 00:08:03.033
Thank you very much
for being so patient.

00:08:03.033 --> 00:08:06.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:06.334 --> 00:08:08.434
Finally, a man in France
set a world record

00:08:08.434 --> 00:08:10.501
for standing
on top of a hot-air balloon

00:08:10.501 --> 00:08:13.033
nearly 12,000 feet in the sky.

00:08:13.033 --> 00:08:14.868
Check this out.

00:08:14.868 --> 00:08:17.000
[ Light laughter ]
-What?

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:19.601
-The only thing more dangerous
is eating the tuna at Subway.

00:08:19.601 --> 00:08:22.133
[ Laughter ]

00:08:22.133 --> 00:08:24.801
When he came back down, he was
like, "Yeah, still no signal."

